From 35f2a0c0df0fd73087fea0ff76f4901b1b14bd90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maksym Paziuk <17340729+virus-on@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:14:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] sophgo: add target for the Sipeed LicheeRV Nano WE

Adds a sophgo target for the SG2002 (RISC-V C906) on mainline Linux 6.18
and one device, the Sipeed LicheeRV Nano WE.

- Boot: the vendor fip.bin (FSBL, OpenSBI, U-Boot) and logo.jpeg, taken
  unmodified from Sipeed's 2025-12-30 image, go on a FAT boot partition
  with boot.sd, an LZMA-compressed FIT using the configuration name the
  vendor U-Boot expects. U-Boot decodes logo.jpeg on every boot and
  crash-loops after a warm reboot without it.
- Device tree for the WE board: memory, SDIO Wi-Fi with its power
  sequence on GPIOA26, Ethernet, the user button on GPIOA30 and a
  restart controller.
- cvitek-ephy: a PHY driver for the internal 10/100 PHY, porting the
  vendor's analog tuning and efuse calibration.
- sophgo-reboot: restart through the RTC warm reset.
- squashfs root with an F2FS overlay, and sysupgrade through the
  legacy-sdcard helpers. Settings travel through the FAT partition.
- First boot: Ethernet is WAN, an empty br-lan is LAN at 192.168.8.1/24,
  flow offloading is on, and the radio becomes the AP "LicheeWRT" once
  the SDIO card shows up, using the key from /etc/licheewrt-wifi-key.
- Kernel command line appends loglevel=4 panic=10, since the vendor
  U-Boot passes loglevel=0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
